## Context

R'nB Startup Hackathon 2022 (RNBC) is a national-level annual student startup competition organized by UKM Research 'n Business (UKM R'nB) Universitas Diponegoro under the theme *"Realizing the Post-Pandemic Economic Growth of Indonesia"*. This website was built as the official public information portal for prospective participants across Indonesian universities.

## Problem

Information for multi-stage national competitions — including competition categories, three-stage selection timelines, bootcamp schedules, FAQs, official guidebooks, and WhatsApp contact persons — is difficult for participants to navigate when scattered across social media posts and chat broadcasts.

## My role

Owner: I designed and built the static multi-page frontend, styled the responsive layout with SCSS/CSS, integrated interactive navigation and scroll animations, and deployed the site to Firebase Hosting.

## As-is analysis

Mapping participant questions showed five primary information needs: an overview of the competition and previous after-movie, detailed event theme and startup categories, stage-by-stage timelines, frequently asked questions, and direct access to the official guidebook PDF and committee contacts.

## Requirements

- Clear multi-page navigation covering Home, About, Event, FAQs, and Information.
- Dedicated pages for competition categories and stage-by-stage timelines (`timeline1` through `timeline9`).
- Direct downloadable official Guidebook (`GuideBook.pdf`) and embedded RNBC 2021 after-movie video tour.
- Direct WhatsApp contact links for committee contact persons and responsive mobile/desktop layout.

## Solution design

The site uses a lightweight, static multi-page architecture so pages load quickly without backend dependencies. Shared navigation and footer patterns keep orientation consistent across overview pages, category details, and timeline breakdowns.

## Build

Built with semantic HTML5, modular SCSS compiled to CSS3, vanilla JavaScript, Remix Icons, and ScrollReveal for smooth section reveals, then deployed on Firebase Hosting at [rnbc-2022.web.app](https://rnbc-2022.web.app/). Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/Website-RNBC](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/Website-RNBC).

## Verification

Verified responsive layout across mobile and desktop viewports, checked all internal navigation links (`home`, `about`, `event`, `faqs`, `information`, and timeline pages), confirmed `GuideBook.pdf` and media assets load properly, and verified live availability on Firebase Hosting.

## Outcome

Delivered a live, publicly accessible competition portal for UKM R'nB Universitas Diponegoro that gave national student teams a single reference point for RNBC 2022 tracks, schedules, FAQs, and guidebook resources.

## Reflection

For time-bound campus and national events, a well-structured static site hosted on Firebase provides reliable uptime, fast loading, and straightforward content updates without the operational overhead of a backend server.
